   "definition_quote": "In each round $t$, the environment generates an i.i.d. random reward vector $\\{r_{t,k}\\}_{k \\in [K]}$ from an unknown fixed distribution. An adversary, having access to the reward vector, subsequently attacks these rewards to produce the corrupted reward vector ... The corruption level is defined as $C = \\sum_{t=1}^T \\max_{k \\in [K]} \\left| \\widetilde{r}_{t,k} - r_{t,k} \\right|$."
